<article class="env-lemma" id="0AJI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AJI">Lemma <span data-tag="0AJI">87.19.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $Y$ be a formal algebraic space over $S$. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a map of sheaves on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ which is representable by algebraic spaces. Then $X$ is a formal algebraic space. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\{ Y_ i \to Y\} $ be as in Definition <a href="/tag/0AIM" data-tag="0AIM">87.11.1</a>. Then $X \times _ Y Y_ i \to X$ is a family of morphisms representable by algebraic spaces, étale, and jointly surjective. Thus it suffices to show that $X \times _ Y Y_ i$ is a formal algebraic space, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0AJ1" data-tag="0AJ1">87.15.1</a>. This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AJH" data-tag="0AJH">87.19.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>